s his third medal of the Sarajevo Winter Olympics, as he had also won a bronze in the 500. Khlebnikov’s time held up for the silver, matching his silver from the 1,000. The bronze went to the Soviet Union’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/84313"} "Oleg Bozhyev"] ", who was competing in his first international meet, but who would, in late March 1984, break the world record in Medeo with 1:53.26."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button44618", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button44618').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "300 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "700 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1100 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "8O"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/84286"} "Gaétan Boucher"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "1:58.36"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "24.50"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "53.60"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1:24.72"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2O"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/87905"} "Sergey Khlebnikov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "1:58.83"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "24.79"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "54.60"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1:25.70"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:t